<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taejong of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1367">1367</a>–<a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Yi Bang-won</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taejong, born Yi Bang-won, was the third king of Joseon, ruling from 1400 to 1418. A son of the founder Taejo, he killed rival princes and the chief minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jeong-do-jeon">Jeong Do-jeon</a> in 1398 before taking the throne. As king he abolished private armies, made the six ministries report directly to the throne and introduced identity tags for men. He abdicated in favour of his son Sejong in 1418 but kept control of the military until his death.</p></div>
